{"name":"Barrel Aged","hex":"#8b6945","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"barrel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A round (cylindrical) vessel, such as a cask, of greater length than breadth, and bulging in the middle, made of staves bound with hoops, and having flat ends (heads). The word is sometimes applied to a similar cylindrical container made of metal, usually called a drum.","Such a cask of a certain size, holding one-eighth of what a tun holds. (See a diagram comparing cask sizes.)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put or to pack in a barrel or barrels.","To move quickly or in an uncontrolled manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barrel"},{"term":"aged","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Old.","Having the age of."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Old people, collectively."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aged"}],"entries":[{"title":"Barrel","blocks":[{"text":"A barrel or cask is a hollow cylindrical container with a bulging center, longer than it is wide. They are traditionally made of wooden staves and bound by wooden or metal hoops. The word vat is often used for large containers for liquids, usually alcoholic beverages; a small barrel or cask is known as a keg."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg/330px-Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barrel"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg/500px-Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg/500px-Oak-wine-barrel-at-toneleria-nacional-chile.jpg?utm_sour